raise those babies yourself.

13:55.268 --> 13:58.203
But as a mom, I don't know
if I can in good conscience

13:58.204 --> 14:00.005
leave this family here.

14:00.006 --> 14:02.708
We'll just have to smuggle
her and her babies back in.

14:02.709 --> 14:05.178
Well, no one's better at
smuggling than El Chapo.

14:05.179 --> 14:06.478
Maybe he can help us.

14:06.479 --> 14:08.597
How are you gonna get El Chapo to help?

14:08.598 --> 14:09.473
It's easy.

14:09.474 --> 14:11.885
All you got to do is say
"dyed black eyebrows"

14:11.886 --> 14:14.153
into the wind, and he appears.

14:14.154 --> 14:16.956
Dyed black eyebrows.

14:16.957 --> 14:18.290
Can I help you?

14:18.291 --> 14:20.025
Peter Gallagher?

14:20.026 --> 14:21.059
Maybe I can help.

14:21.060 --> 14:22.361
Mark Cuban?

14:22.362 --> 14:24.639
Oh, we're getting all
the wrong eyebrow guys.

14:29.327 --> 14:31.445
Mrs. Griffin, you would take the risk

14:31.446 --> 14:34.081
of smuggling me and my
children across the border?

14:34.082 --> 14:36.084
But you could be arrested.

14:36.085 --> 14:38.819
I realize that, but you
have just as much right

14:38.820 --> 14:41.388
to a decent life for your
children as anyone else.

14:41.389 --> 14:43.090
Now we just need a plan.

14:43.091 --> 14:44.825
All right, what if we...

14:44.826 --> 14:45.826
run!

14:45.827 --> 14:47.495
Damn it, Peter!

14:47.496 --> 14:49.097
What about Quagmire?

14:49.098 --> 14:50.898
He could probably get
his hands on a plane.

14:50.899 --> 14:52.834
Lois, that's actually a great idea.

14:52.835 --> 14:53.850
"Actually"?

14:53.851 --> 14:55.310
W-Why are you saying it like that?

14:55.311 --> 14:57.604
And Quagmire owes me a
favor anyway, remember?

14:57.605 --> 15:00.460
Last time he went out of town,
I sat on his eggs for him.

15:01.442 --> 15:03.161
Peter, it's time for lunch.

15:03.162 --> 15:06.062
Sorry, Lois, can't leave the
eggs till Quagmire gets back.

15:06.063 --> 15:08.398
We're having sloppy joes.

15:08.399 --> 15:11.152
Well, I guess I haven't seen
that mongoose in a while.

15:12.419 --> 15:13.838
We're having sloppy joes.

15:13.839 --> 15:14.839
Yeah, I heard.

15:14.840 --> 15:16.107
Please say you got the onion bun...

15:16.108 --> 15:17.675
<i>We're having sloppy joes.</i>

15:17.676 --> 15:19.528
Mongoose!

15:21.295 --> 15:22.597
Mongeese!

15:31.005 --> 15:33.824
Hey, just a heads-up, my
dad's friend, Mr. Quagmire,

15:33.825 --> 15:35.593
is gonna say a lot of stuff to you,

15:35.594 --> 15:37.594
and it's all gonna be disgusting.

15:37.595 --> 15:38.829
Hey, you must be Isabella.

15:38.830 --> 15:40.464
I came as soon as I heard about you.

15:40.465 --> 15:41.833
And then I got on my plane.

15:41.834 --> 15:43.200
All right.

15:43.201 --> 15:44.318
Hold it right there!

15:46.053 --> 15:47.604
Uh-oh. Somebody's coming.

15:47.605 --> 15:48.939
N-Now, hold on, hold on.

15:48.940 --> 15:51.508
I put my business card in a
fishbowl at an El Torito.

15:51.509 --> 15:52.769
This could be about that.

15:54.412 --> 15:56.372
<i>Polic├нa! Put your hands up!</i>

15:56.914 --> 15:58.873
Is this about the raffle
for the free lunch?

15:58.874 --> 16:00.809
Does it have to be during
the week, because I...

16:00.810 --> 16:01.877
Aah!

16:01.878 --> 16:03.780
Wait a second, are we being arrested?

16:03.781 --> 16:05.214
We've done nothing wrong.

16:05.215 --> 16:06.648
We're not arresting you.

16:06.649 --> 16:08.234
We're taking your plane.

16:11.971 --> 16:14.507
And, Javier, get their
keys and take their SUV.

16:19.980 --> 16:23.050
Ah, that stupid, fat guido.

16:23.051 --> 16:25.001
No, Peter, that's the wrong racial slur.

16:25.002 --> 16:27.770
No, I know, I was just
thinking about Snooki.

16:33.692 --> 16:36.912
Boy, I can't believe there'd
be corrupt cops in Mexico.

16:36.913 --> 16:39.348
Yeah, Donald Trump was right:

16:39.349 --> 16:41.917
his daughter is a hot piece of ass.

16:41.918 --> 16:43.986
Uh, you guys, don't panic,

16:43.987 --> 16:45.954
but there's a couple
of coyotes over there.

16:47.857 --> 16:50.792
<i>Oh, like Coyote Ugly with Piper Perabo.</i>

16:50.793 --> 16:51.928
Peh... I-is that it?

16:51.929 --> 16:53.295
Peh-Peh-ree... Peh-ree-bow?

16:53.296 --> 16:55.931
Peh-Pera... Pera-Pera-boo?

16:55.932 --> 16:57.099
Pera-boo? Say it with me.

16:57.100 --> 16:58.700
Per-Per-a-bow.

16:58.701 --> 16:59.559
Is that right?

16:59.560 --> 17:01.019
It's weird, but you remember.

17:01.020 --> 17:02.020
You know? I guess...

17:02.021 --> 17:03.396
I guess that's the point.

17:03.397 --> 17:05.148
Do you think she's set for life?

17:05.149 --> 17:06.942
Peter, we're about to die!

17:09.196 --> 17:10.813
No, my babies!

17:10.814 --> 17:12.047
Get out of here!

17:12.048 --> 17:13.234
You leave them alone!

17:13.867 --> 17:15.951
Ow!

17:15.952 --> 17:16.985
Ah! Chris!

17:23.842 --> 17:26.562
You guys, I've been bit!

17:26.563 --> 17:28.864
And it got away with my
friendship bracelet.

17:28.865 --> 17:30.732
You are a boy.

17:30.733 --> 17:33.001
Chris, you saved my babies.

17:33.002 --> 17:35.003
Oh, my God, Peter, we did nothing.

17:35.004 --> 17:36.872
We're his parents and we did nothing.

17:36.873 --> 17:38.140
I know, but, wow,

17:38.141 --> 17:40.242
did you see how Chris
took care of those kids?

17:40.243 --> 17:42.578
Up till now, the only thing
he could take care of

17:42.579 --> 17:44.146
was my traffic tickets.

17:44.147 --> 17:46.748
- Name?
- Uh, Peter Griffin.

17:46.749 --> 17:48.150
Peter Griffin's here to surrender

17:48.151 --> 17:49.885
for his vehicular manslaughter.

17:49.886 --> 17:51.186
What? No.

17:51.187 --> 17:52.406
I'm a good boy!

17:53.941 --> 17:55.741
He is a good boy.

18:01.014 --> 18:02.364
Oh, this is awful.

18:02.365 --> 18:03.732
Chris is injured,

18:03.733 --> 18:05.576
and we're completely
out of food and water.

18:05.577 --> 18:06.201
I know.

18:06.202 --> 18:09.271
I'm so thirsty, I'd be willing
to drink anyone's pee.

18:09.272 --> 18:11.341
Not-Not yours, Chris or Peter.

18:11.342 --> 18:13.242
But, you know, you know, anyone.

18:13.243 --> 18:16.379
Mom, Dad, thanks for trying to help.

18:16.380 --> 18:18.715
You know, I just wanted
to do the right thing,

18:18.716 --> 18:21.049
but now we're all gonna die.

18:21.050 --> 18:23.118
Did-Did you gals hear my pee thing?

18:27.540 --> 18:30.259
Time for clean getaway.

18:30.260 --> 18:32.227
<i>- Consuela?
- ┬┐T├нa?</i>

18:32.228 --> 18:33.729
<i>Ay, thank God.</i>

18:33.730 --> 18:35.097
How did you find us?

18:35.098 --> 18:37.116
Babies' earring have chip.

18:40.719 --> 18:42.037
Oh, well, this is great.

18:42.038 --> 18:43.805
Can you help us get to the border?

18:43.806 --> 18:46.241
Oh, you already in United States.

18:46.242 --> 18:47.242
We are?

18:47.243 --> 18:48.978
Yes, this Texas.

18:48.979 --> 18:50.279
What?

18:50.280 --> 18:52.147
S-So, wait, so we walked
right across the border

18:52.148 --> 18:53.423
and didn't even know it?

18:53.424 --> 18:54.841
That is a problem.

18:54.842 --> 18:55.926
Right?

18:55.927 --> 18:58.153
I mean, politics aside,
we can all agree,

18:58.154 --> 18:59.806
that is a problem.

19:03.842 --> 19:05.294
Thanks for the ride, Consuela.

19:05.295 --> 19:08.064
And thanks for talking us on
that little detour to Dollywood.

19:08.065 --> 19:10.400
Was I right, or was I right?

19:10.401 --> 19:12.319
Yep, totally worth the extra two days.

19:13.820 --> 19:16.305
Look, Chris, I owe you an apology.

19:16.306 --> 19:17.864
I didn't believe in you.

19:17.865 --> 19:20.409
I was wrong to say you couldn't
handle the responsibility

19:20.410 --> 19:22.010
of taking care of two kids.

19:22.011 --> 19:24.279
Y-You risked your life for those babies.

19:24.280 --> 19:26.181
Well, I didn't want them to get hurt.

19:26.182 --> 19:27.316
That's right.

19:27.317 --> 19:29.117
Because you care about them,

19:29.118 --> 19:31.286
just like you care about Isabella.

19:31.287 --> 19:33.288
And if you want to continue to date her

19:33.289 --> 19:34.823
and be a part of those kids' lives,

19:34.824 --> 19:37.292
I'd be just fine with that.

19:37.293 --> 19:39.027
Are you kidding? Screw that.

19:39.028 --> 19:40.929
Looking after babies is a nightmare.

19:40.930 --> 19:42.847
Oh, you have no idea.

19:42.848 --> 19:45.133
You know how many times I
had you kids in the oven,

19:45.134 --> 19:46.935
just daring myself to turn it on?

19:46.936 --> 19:50.773
Well, thanks for trusting me
to figure it out for myself.

19:50.774 --> 19:52.141
I love you, Mom.

19:52.142 --> 19:54.395
I love you, too, sweetheart.

19:59.966 --> 20:03.051
Isabella, being with you
has been really great.

20:03.052 --> 20:05.054
But I think I realized my mom was right.

20:05.055 --> 20:08.023
I'm too young to be taking
on this much responsibility.

20:08.024 --> 20:09.558
I understand.

20:09.559 --> 20:13.328
But I know someday you will
make an incredible father.

20:13.329 --> 20:14.496
Good-bye, Chris.

20:14.497 --> 20:16.250
Good-bye, Isabella.

20:23.639 --> 20:25.341
Chris, time for dinner.

20:25.342 --> 20:27.175
We're having sloppy joes.

20:27.176 --> 20:28.510
Oh, boy!

20:28.511 --> 20:30.412
We're having sloppy joes.

20:30.413 --> 20:31.832
Yeah, I heard you.

20:33.366 --> 20:34.717
Oh, dear God.

20:34.718 --> 20:36.084
Oh, they're all dead.

20:36.085 --> 20:38.353
No, please, no!

20:40.948 --> 20:45.448
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:46.111 --> 20:48.014
<i> We're having sloppy joes.</i>

20:49.114 --> 20:50.851
<i>We're having sloppy joes.</i>

20:52.051 --> 20:53.354
<i>We're having sloppy joes.</i>